    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0354" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500. CC/7–545</note>
                <head>No. 184 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Balfour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Director of European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Matthews</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05">July 5th, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Doc</hi>, I send you herewith a paraphrase of a
                    telegram just received from London in which the addition of two subjects to the
                    agenda for <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terminal</hi> is suggested.</p>
                <p>Would you let me know whether the United States Government have any comments on
                    these suggestions.</p>
                <p>Yours ever</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jock Balfour</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d184-a1.xml" xpointer="d184-a1"/>
            </div>
